{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>לא יחרוך</b> — A deceitful man does not roast his game, nor does he cook it, for it will be robbed from him." "<b>והון אדם</b> — draws after it [its] meaning [i.e. its interpretation]: the wealth of a man that is precious and not plundered, it is the wealth of a diligent man, who travels about for trade for his livelihood, and he does not deceive."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The phrase מושך אחר עמו is obscure; read hyper-literally as 'draws after it its people/meaning,' though the text may be corrupt (perhaps מושך אחר עניינו, 'draws after its matter')."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:28.082801611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}